  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$How can the principles of kindness and empathy, as described in the poem, be applied in daily life?$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$Reflect on the idea that 'you help it live' when you touch a heart. What does 'live' signify here?$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true);
INSERT INTO public.question_bank (id, institution_id, subject_id, topic_id, grade_level_id, class_group_id, question_text, question_type, options, correct_answer, marks, difficulty_level, tags, source, created_by, is_approved, parent_question_id, sub_question_count, sequence_order) VALUES
  ('9fbe9834-2dc7-4214-a7b2-3541ed3a2be4', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The "Gift Of The Season" unit aims to cultivate empathy and community spirit among students. A core component is an activity where students reflect on personal experiences of altruism. For instance, one student documented organizing a fundraiser to procure school supplies for a disadvantaged classmate. This initiative not only addressed a tangible need but also instilled a profound sense of pride and value in the student, underscoring the potent impact of collective community support. Concurrently, the accompanying poem, "Gift Of The Season," poetically reinforces these values, positing that the true essence of the festive period lies not in material acquisitions but in acts of genuine kindness, such as offering a warm beverage or a comforting blanket.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 10, NULL),
  ('55c7855c-d38a-42ee-b7be-c2607b1d8062', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The small town of Willow Creek faced a challenging winter. A severe snowstorm had left many elderly residents isolated, and the local food bank was struggling with dwindling donations. Amidst this hardship, a group of high school students, inspired by a school project on the power of kindness, decided to act. They started by simply clearing snow from their neighbors' driveways, often leaving a warm, homemade cookie. This 'eaglow' of generosity quickly spread. A local café owner, seeing the students' dedication, offered free hot cocoa to anyone volunteering. Soon, the entire community was involved: some donated 'fragrant' baked goods to the food bank, others repaired 'frosty' pipes for those without heat, and a retired carpenter organized a workshop to fix broken furniture, restoring items to a 'renewed' state. The town, once feeling the 'pain' of isolation, began to feel a sense of unity and warmth, as if a 'starlit' night had brought forth a new dawn.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 25, NULL),
  ('48a46b58-958e-46ae-b2f4-0b5bc85c1e1c', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$The poem "Gift Of The Season" meticulously constructs a winter and Christmas tableau, moving beyond mere superficial festivity to explore the profound core of the season. It vividly describes "lights aglow on frosty eves" and "candles flicker, soft and warm," establishing an ambiance of serene beauty and gentle guidance. Fundamentally, the poem declares that the authentic spirit is not embodied by "parcels wrapped in bows" but by "a simpler, deeper mirth, Found in the act of giving's birth." This central tenet is substantiated by concrete examples of compassionate gestures, such as the sharing of cocoa or the provision of a blanket, thereby asserting that genuine human connection and altruism constitute the most invaluable gifts.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 10, NULL),
  ('7b3b8037-de9a-4d5b-9393-7e5dfec28685', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '289adc99-0a65-48fc-82ac-0bbbc000b660', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$A smile offered to a stranger’s face, Love’s quiet presence fills space. From hands that give without a thought, To hearts that swell with joy untaught, The gifts we share from deep within, Spark the brightest light there’s been. For as we give, so do we gain, A world renewed, washed free from pain, Each act of kindness, small or grand, Weaves an embroidery so grand. So let the spirit freely flow, As Christmas lights in windows glow, And remember, in each gift you give, You touch a heart, you help it live.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-949Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 25, NULL);
